  "interpretation": "Parmenides invites looking together at Greatness itself and the other great things in the same way; Socrates concedes a further common greatness. The literal same-predication reconstruction is tested, without attributing universal self-predication to every dialogue or excluding an essential-characterization reply. Bounded reading of the materialized Greek witness. Retained as prose; it is not silently equated with the stronger universal Lean reconstruction.",
